        # ReleaseNotes of this module
        ReleaseNotes = 'What''s New in v1.0.29

Full release notes: https://github.com/jullienl/HPE-COM-PowerShell-Library/releases/tag/v1.0.29



NEW CMDLETS

- Get-HPECOMGroupServerHardwareVerification: returns the hardware verification status of the servers in a group and, with -ShowChanges, the components added, removed or modified since the last accepted baseline.
- Approve-HPECOMGroupServerHardwareChange: accepts the hardware changes of servers in a group so their current hardware becomes the new trusted baseline.
- Get-HPECOMFirmwareAnalysisReport: returns the Compute Ops Management firmware analysis report against the latest baselines: servers and components to update, servers up to date or not analyzed, and the security bulletins and customer advisories resolved by the update.
- Get-HPEGLPermission: lists the permissions that can be used in custom roles.
- New-HPEGLCustomRole: creates a custom role from permissions, from an existing role (-BasedOnRole), or both.
- Set-HPEGLCustomRole: renames a custom role, changes its description, adds, removes or replaces permissions.
- Remove-HPEGLCustomRole: deletes custom roles; built-in roles are protected.



BUG FIXES

- Get-HPEGLRole: -ServiceName ''GreenLake Platform'' now works, so the permissions and assigned users of platform roles, including custom roles, can be listed.
- Get-HPECOMServer -ShowSecurityParameters: the OverallSecurityStatus column is no longer empty.
- New-HPEGLSubscription: clear message when the subscription key is already claimed in another workspace, with the workspace name or ID.



IMPROVEMENTS

- Get-HPEGLRole: the Type column now shows Custom for custom roles.
- New-HPECOMSettingiLOSettings / Set-HPECOMSettingiLOSettings: new -HardwareVerification parameter.
- Get-HPECOMServer -ShowSecurityParameters: new iLOSecurityStatus and HardwareVerification columns.
- Get-HPECOMGroup: new -ShowSecurityStatus switch with per-group security and hardware verification counts.
- Get-HPEGLAPICredential: new -AllUsers switch that lists the personal API clients of all users of the workspace (administrators).

